body:
@teehamaral It works sometimes, just because it was coincidental. If you have less number of groups, then its more likely that the results might come in correct order, but this will not always be the case. If you check the sample I had provided, the first 4 group tasks returned in same order and only after that, the order got messed up.

To get rid of this problem, I just assigned an index to all the group tasks while calling it and, returned this index along with the task's results. Later, when all the group tasks were finished, I just sorted the results according to that index. A totally dirty solution, but couldn't come up with anything else since it was an urgent requirement for me.

But, I'm not sure how you got this problem in v3.x though.
